{"id": "L10", "command": "submit", "inputs": {"recommendation": {"decision": "keep", "challenger": null, "diagnosis": "The champion's error rose in the recent development period, driven by a March spike and large BR misses, with opposite-signed biases across corridors (IN forecast too low, BR and MX too high). Faster refits, shorter windows, simpler models, a different tree family and a leaner feature set all failed to beat it, so the deterioration looks like a harder market rather than a fixable config problem.", "evidence": [{"claim": "The champion's error over the last 26 weeks was 52.66 bps vs 43.31 bps before (+21.59%).", "ledger_ids": ["L02"]}, {"claim": "Champion bias differs in sign by corridor: IN 12.62 bps (forecasts too low) vs BR -12.73 bps and MX -7.37 bps (forecasts too high).", "ledger_ids": ["L03"]}, {"claim": "Refitting weekly instead of monthly was slightly worse: 52.76 bps vs 52.66 bps (+0.19%), and also shortening the window to 1y was worse at 55.41 bps (+5.22%).", "ledger_ids": ["L04", "L05"]}, {"claim": "Simpler models were worse: ridge at 54.22 bps (+2.96%) and the EWMA baseline at 56.37 bps (+7.05%), the latter with a BR breach rate of 0.139.", "ledger_ids": ["L07", "L06"]}, {"claim": "The closest alternatives were still worse than the champion: LightGBM at 53.18 bps (+0.99%) and a lean xgboost without fx and dollar features at 52.87 bps (+0.4%), both within noise.", "ledger_ids": ["L08", "L09"]}], "risks": "If the corridor biases reflect a persistent shift in customer markups, a model that adapts its level faster could start to outperform, and keeping a long-window model would leave that gain unrealised. The champion's IN error has also been rising recently, which could signal a corridor-specific regime change.", "watch_next_week": "Watch whether the IN under-forecast bias and the BR over-forecast bias persist or grow, whether markups keep falling across corridors, and whether recent-weeks IN error keeps rising; if so, test markup-focused or corridor-adaptive configs."}}, "result": {"accepted": true, "errors": [], "attempt": 1}, "time": "2026-11-15T12:12:11Z"}
